.\" Hand-written sections of improv-gui(1); crates/cli/src/man.rs adds the rest.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B improv-gui
opens a model in a NeXTSTEP-style workspace: an application menu, one
worksheet window per matrix, and a model browser. Pivot by dragging a
category tile between a worksheet's strips; edit an input cell by
double-clicking it; add a formula by typing
.I Name = formula
on the last line of a worksheet's formula list. Every change is saved as it
is made. Without an argument the model is in memory only.
.PP
A model is a store file made by
.BR improv (1),
a Postgres model URL,
.BI postgres:// user @ host / db ?model= name\fR,
or the URL of an
.BR improv-server (1),
.BI https:// host\fR[\fB: port\fR][\fI/prefix\fR][\fB?sslrootcert=\fIFILE\fR]
.RB ( http://
only to this machine). A server model opens the web GUI's worksheets in
the window, as the user its token names: what the server's access
policies hide is absent, derived cells are the server's, what the user
may not do is greyed out, and a refused change says why. Changes made
elsewhere show as they happen. The certificate is checked against the
operating system's CAs, or only against
.IR FILE .
.SH KEYS
Key equivalents take Ctrl (Cmd on macOS):
.BR s " save, " z " undo, " Z " or " y " redo, " h " hide, " q " quit."
In a grid: arrows or
.B hjkl
move, Shift+arrows select a range (the status bar shows its sum), Enter or
F2 edits,
.BR [ " and " ]
(or PageUp and PageDown) page,
.B n
and Shift+\fBn\fR cycle the measure forward and back.
.PP
F1, anywhere (a formula edit included), or
.B Help \(-> Functions...
opens the function help: a search over the built-in functions by name,
alias or description, the matches grouped by category, and the selected
one's signature, category, aliases, description and argument types.
Up and Down move the selection; Enter, a double-click or
.B Insert
puts
.I NAME(
into the formula last edited, at its caret. F1 again closes it.
.PP
In a formula edit, a name being typed drops a list of matching functions,
measures and categories: Up and Down select, Tab or Enter accepts
(a function as
.IR NAME( ),
Esc closes the list; with the list closed Enter commits. The rest of the
selected name, or inside a call the parameters still to give, trail the
caret in gray, and a tooltip shows the signature with the current
argument in bold.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IMPROV_API_TOKEN
The bearer token for a server model; without it the window asks for one.
It is kept in memory only.
.TP
.B IMPROV_LOCALE
The formula locale (else the OS locale): formulas are shown and typed in
it, e.g. German names, a decimal comma and
.B ;
separators for
.BR de .
.TP
.B MENTAT_MMAP_SIZE
As for
.BR improv (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
improv-gui sample.db
IMPROV_API_TOKEN=$TOKEN improv-gui https://improv.example.com
improv-gui 'postgres://me@127.0.0.1/sales?sslmode=disable&model=plan'
.fi
.SH AUTHOR
Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-files (5),
.BR improv-formulas (7),
.BR improv-tui (1),
.BR improv-server (1).
